{"name":"Plum Blossom Dye","hex":"#b48a76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit and its tree.\n An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nA stone-fruit tree which bears this fruit, Prunus domestica. \nThe edible, fleshy stone fruit of several species resembling the plum, or the tree from which they grow. \nPrunus sect. Prunus\nPrunus cerasifera (cherry plum or myrobalan).\nPrunus salicina (Chinese plum or Japanese plum).\nPrunus spinosa (sloe).\nPrunus ursina (bear's plum).\nPrunus sect. Prunocerasus (North American plums)\nPrunus americana (American plum).\nPrunus angustifolia (Chickasaw plum or sand plum).\nPrunus hortulana (hortulan plum).\nPrunus nigra (Canadian plum or black plum).\nPrunus rivularis (creek plum or hog plum).\nPrunus subcordata (Klamath plum or Oregon plum).\nPrunus sect. Armeniaca (better known as apricots)\nPrunus mume, an Asian fruit more closely related to the apricot than the plum, usually consumed pickled, dried, or as a juice or wine; ume.\n A dried grape or raisin, as used in a pudding or cake.","An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark bluish-red colour.","Choice; especially lavish or preferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum"},{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"dye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorant, especially one that has an affinity to the substrate to which it is applied.","Any hue or color."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To colour with dye, or as if with dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus mume","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus mume, also known as a Chinese plum, is a tree species in the family Rosaceae. It is also referenced by its flowers as plum blossom. Although referred to as a plum in English, it is classified in the Armeniaca section of the genus Prunus, making it an apricot. Mei flowers, or meihua (梅花), which bloom in the late winter and early spring, notably during the spring festival (春節), symbolize endurance, as they are the first to bloom despite the cold; the flower is one of the Three Friends of Winter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Prunus_mume.JPG/330px-Prunus_mume.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_mume","wikidata":"Q157763"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom","wikidata":"Q2047589"},{"title":"Dye","blocks":[{"text":"A dye is a colored substance that is soluble in some solvent; by contrast pigments are insoluble or nearly so in all solvents. Because of their solubility, dyes can chemically bind to the material they color. Dye is generally applied in an aqueous solution and may require a mordant to improve the fastness of the dye on the fiber."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg/330px-2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dye","wikidata":"Q189720"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/120px-Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/250px-Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg/120px-Prunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrunus_mume_fruits_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_washed_and_stemmed.jpg/120px-Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_washed_and_stemmed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_washed_and_stemmed.jpg/250px-Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_washed_and_stemmed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_washed_and_stemmed.jpg/120px-Maesil_%28prunus_mume%29_wash